	(text "The DS1315 has two battery inputs. BAT1 is connected to the RTC battery which \ncan be equipped on the CPU card. Optionally you can connect BAT1 to the VBAT\nfrom the Q-BUS64, either using the battery as the backup battery for RAM as\nwell, or without battery using the backup battery connected to VBAT. Another\noption is to use the battery on the CPU card for the RTC and additionally \nconnect VBAT from Q-BUS 64 to BAT2. Else BAT2 needs to be connected to GND\nusing the solder jumper."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 77.47 31.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8bf360d8-f50b-4bb0-b161-3a5c110158ee")
	)
	(text "ROM/~{RAM} needs to be connected to GND in order for to work together\nwith the circuit and the way the DS1215 is connected on the KDJ11E.\nAlso ~{RST} should be connected either to INIT or to VCCO in order\nto avoid problems with the initial programming."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.03 109.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "aab69d41-23ba-4cc1-95b4-6629b2eb0625")
	)
